<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="003" project="dotnet-10-upgrade-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Retarget Spaarke.Core + Spaarke.Dataverse; required package moves + pin removals</title>
    <phase>P0 Retarget + build-green</phase>
    <gate>002 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .csproj + runtime-tied packages (Dataverse.Client/MSAL/Identity.Web); brownfield; tags include bff-api.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Enumerated package moves from design §6.1/§6.2; bounded judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Serial P0 chain; BFF (004) references these libs, so they must retarget first and coherently.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>002</deps>
    <tags>dotnet, migration, packages, dataverse, auth, bff-api</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Retarget `Spaarke.Core` and `Spaarke.Dataverse` from net8.0 to net10.0 and land the required package moves: align all `Microsoft.Extensions.*` to the 10.0.x wave, bump `Microsoft.PowerPlatform.Dataverse.Client` 1.1.32 → 1.2.26 (drags MSAL ≥ 4.84.2), bump `Microsoft.Identity.Web` (+`.MicrosoftGraph`) → 4.14.2, and remove the superseded CVE-pin `PackageReference`s (same STJ/Asn1/Pkcs/RegEx set) after confirming inbox ≥ pin. Zero behavior change — this is `ServiceClient` same-API-surface work.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Dataverse ServiceClient, MSAL/Identity.Web auth stacks, and Microsoft.Extensions version alignment. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`Spaarke.Core.csproj` + `Spaarke.Dataverse.csproj` target `net10.0`; `Microsoft.Extensions.*` all at 10.0.x; `Dataverse.Client` 1.2.26; MSAL ≥ 4.84.2; `Identity.Web`(+`.MicrosoftGraph`) 4.14.2; superseded CVE pins removed; `dotnet build -c Release` green for both libs; no NU1605 version-unification warnings.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>design §3.1/§6.1/§6.2. `Spaarke.Dataverse` pins `Dataverse.Client 1.1.32` — a pre-net8 pin whose asset resolves an out-of-support-runtime asset on net10; 1.2.x (added the net8 target in 1.2.1/1.2.2) is the same `ServiceClient` API surface. Both libs carry the same STJ + CVE pins as Scheduling (task 002 already produced the inbox-≥-pin evidence — reuse it). Ending the 8.0/10.0 Extensions split-brain is the point (M.E.AI 10.x already pulls 10.x abstractions transitively).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Spaarke.Core.csproj</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Spaarke.Dataverse.csproj</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/pin-removals.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">Directory.Packages.props</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="002" status="pending">Scheduling retargeted; pin-removal evidence available to reuse.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: ONLY Core + Dataverse csproj (+ any shared version catalog entries they consume). BFF (004) and tests (005) are separate tasks.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Required moves are exact (spec FR-03): Extensions → 10.0.x (current 10.0.10); Dataverse.Client → 1.2.26; MSAL ≥ 4.84.2 (target 4.87.0); Identity.Web + .MicrosoftGraph → 4.14.2. No optional major-version bumps here.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Remove superseded CVE pins ONLY after confirming inbox ≥ pin (reuse task 002 evidence); keep any pin the framework does not supply.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">The Dataverse.Client / MSAL / Identity.Web bumps are same-major, API-preserving — auth behavior (OBO + MI) MUST be unchanged; do not alter token acquisition flows.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">No AI-internal types introduced; retarget only.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Dataverse ServiceClient + MSAL/Identity.Web version alignment on net10</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="required-package-moves" location="projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md">design §6.1 table — exact from→to for each required package.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load spec FR-01/FR-03/FR-04 + design §6.1/§6.2. Declare RIGOR: FULL.</step>
    <step order="1">Set `<TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>` on both Core and Dataverse csproj.</step>
    <step order="2">Bump `Dataverse.Client` 1.1.32 → 1.2.26 in `Spaarke.Dataverse`; let it drag MSAL ≥ 4.84.2 (target 4.87.0) — verify the resolved MSAL floor.</step>
    <step order="3">Align every `Microsoft.Extensions.*` reference to 10.0.x; bump `Identity.Web` (+`.MicrosoftGraph`) → 4.14.2.</step>
    <step order="4">Remove superseded CVE pins (reuse task 002 inbox-≥-pin evidence); append any new evidence to `notes/pin-removals.md`.</step>
    <step order="5">`dotnet build -c Release` both libs; resolve any NU1605 version-unification warning by aligning versions (not by suppression).</step>
    <step order="6">Run the Dataverse seam integration test if runnable at this stage; otherwise note it is validated in task 030.</step>
    <step order="7">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 003 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation in `projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the Dataverse.Client 1.1→1.2 bump surfaces a non-trivial `ServiceClient` API change (not the expected same-surface), STOP and surface per CLAUDE.md §6 — the spec assumed low code impact; a real API break is a scope change.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build + restore Core/Dataverse</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="config">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Spaarke.Core.csproj</output>
    <output type="config">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Spaarke.Dataverse.csproj</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/pin-removals.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the retargeted libs, `dotnet build -c Release` for both is green with no NU1605 version-unification warnings.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet list package` shows no `Microsoft.Extensions.*` at 8.0.x in Core/Dataverse; `Dataverse.Client` = 1.2.26; MSAL ≥ 4.84.2; `Identity.Web` = 4.14.2.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every removed pin has inbox-≥-CVE evidence recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no token-acquisition (OBO/MI) code path is altered — the change is TFM + package versions only.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec FR-01/FR-03/FR-04. Dataverse seam integration test is the FR-03 acceptance proof — if not runnable until the BFF retargets, defer its execution to task 030 and note that here.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
